Author: Anirudha Talmale <anirudhatalmale6@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 17 12:27:20 2026 +0000

    Revert the typography standardisation; it is held from this release
    
    Instruction: IELPS Public Landing Routing, Webhook & QA Amendment,
    17 August 2026, section 6 — "Typography must be reverted from this build.
    Typography waits for its own separate approval." Section 14 records it as
    REVERT; NOT IN THIS RELEASE.
    
    Commit 25e11de carried two instructions at once: the pathway-first routing
    correction, which is approved and stays, and the typography standardisation,
    which is not. Only the typography half is undone here.
    
    Reverted to their 25e11de^ state:
    
      app/globals.css        --font-sans returns to Inter; --font-display returns
                             to Bricolage over Inter; --font-content is removed.
      app/layout.tsx         Hanken Grotesk is no longer loaded and no longer sits
                             on <html>.
      app/access/page.tsx    Plus Jakarta Sans is loaded again, as the approved
      app/levels/[level]     16 August package supplied it. This is the "one
                             deliberate departure" 25e11de raised for approval;
                             approval did not come, so it goes back.
      lesson-player.tsx      The font-content wrapper around StepScreen is removed.
      preview/lesson-...     The font-content wrapper around the screens is removed.
    
    Kept, because they are approved and unrelated to typography:
    
      start-level-button.tsx  "Continue with <level>" -> /?level=<code>#pathways
      level-band.tsx          "Continue with <level>" -> #pathways; no secondary
                              "Choose a pathway instead"
      cefr-panel.tsx          placement link -> /#pathways
      site-header, access-header, hero, page.tsx, placement-explainer,
      placement-test          the 17 August placement-control removal
    
    Verified in a browser against the built standalone output: the panel home and
    the lesson player compute to Inter for interface text and Bricolage Grotesque
    for display; the Access Panel and the six level pages compute to Plus Jakarta
    Sans, exactly as the approved 16 August package. No Hanken Grotesk and no
    font-content remains anywhere in app/ or components/. The approved copy and
    routing are unchanged: "Continue with A1" still resolves to #pathways, the
    panel header still carries only Pathways and Adult flow, and no Placement
    control has come back. next build clean.

